<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2754" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτ-έω</span></b>  (
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴτημι</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			155
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Theoc.
			28.5
		</span></i>), 
			Ion.
		
		impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴτεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
				</span></i>
			: fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτήσω</span>: aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾔτησα</span>: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾔτηκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Jo.</u>
					5.15
				</span></i>
			: plpf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾐτήκει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>An.</u>
					6.15.5
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			
				Pass.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾔτημαι</span>, etc.:—<i>ask,
				beg</i>, abs., <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				341
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> mostly c. acc.
			rei, <i>ask for, demand</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.358
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.365
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδὸν αἰ.</span>
			<i>ask leave</i> to depart, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.17
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. τινί τι</span>
			<i>to ask</i> something for one, <i><span class="en">
				20.74
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.17
			</span></i>: c. acc. pers. et rei, <i>ask</i> a person <i>for</i> a
			thing, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.295
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.387
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.1
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκας αἰ. τινὰ φόνου</span>
			<i>to demand</i> satisfaction from one for . . , <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.114
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. τι πρός τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					556
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρά τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					1.3.16
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ αἰτήματα ἃ ἡ̓τήκαμεν παρ᾽ αὐτοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Jo.</u>
					5.15
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. acc. pers.
			et inf., <i>ask</i> one <i>to</i> do, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.173
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1334
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ant.</u>
				65
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. παρά τινος δοῦναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Erx.</u>
					398e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> c. acc. only,
				<i>beg of</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				6.49
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> in Logic,
				<i>postulate, assume</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APr.</u>
				41b9
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Top.</u>
				163a6
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>ask for one's own use, claim</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λύσανδρον ἄρχοντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					12.59
				</span></i>
			; freq. almost = the 
				Act.
			, and with the same construct., first in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.90
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρ-</span>), <i><span class="en">
				9.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				822
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτεῖσθαί τινα ὅπως . .
			</span> Antiphol.<i><span class="en">
				12
			</span></i> codd.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάλαισμα μἠποτε λῦσαι θεὸν αἰτοῦμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					880
				</span></i>
			; freq. abs. in part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτουμένψ μοι δός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					480
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				260
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				63
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτουμένη που τεύξεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					778
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτησάμενος ἐχρήσατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					19.27
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ πῦρ γὰρ αἰτῶν, οὐδὲ λοπάδ᾽
					αἰτούμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					476
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτεῖσθαι ὑπέρ τινος</span>
			<i>to beg</i> for one, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				14.22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, of persons, <i>have a thing begged of</i> one, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτηθέντες χρήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.111
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.97
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτεύμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					14.63
				</span></i>
			: c. inf., <i>to be asked to</i> do a thing,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				8(7).5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of things,
				<i>to be asked</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ αἰτεόμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.112
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵπποι ᾐτημένοι</span>
			<i>borrowed</i> horses, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				24.12
			</span></i>.</div>
